3.5  Final Output Description
The model produces two final outputs saved as PLY (polygon file format) point cloud files:
●	vroom_global.ply — The 3D point cloud of the Monaco circuit. Points are coloured by confidence — red = high confidence (road surface, barriers), green = medium, approaching zero = noise. When viewed from above, the point cloud shows the track layout matching the known Monaco circuit map.
●	vroom_camera_path.ply — The recovered camera trajectory — one 3D point per frame, coloured blue. This is the racing line: the optimal path through each corner that minimises lap time. The path visibly follows the geometric racing line (late braking, apex, early exit) through well-reconstructed corners.
✓  Final output: a navigable 3D model of the track and a verified racing line, derived entirely from monocular onboard video with no external sensors. Individual chunk alignment losses consistently below 0.010, indicating high-quality local reconstruction throughout.
